WEBVTT

00:06.040 --> 00:09.560
Whoa! Isn't it beautiful, Oushi?

00:09.560 --> 00:12.570
What's fun about fireworks? 
They're just loud and smoky.

00:12.570 --> 00:13.450
Huh?

00:13.450 --> 00:15.900
What was that? I couldn't hear you!

00:23.710 --> 00:26.250
<b>Oushi
Video Call</b>

01:57.220 --> 02:00.970
Oushi's World

02:03.990 --> 02:05.470
<i>Is he gonna...</i>

02:05.470 --> 02:12.230
<b>Sign Language Guide</b>

02:05.890 --> 02:10.270
<i>update this notebook 
with the stuff I taught him today?</i>

02:12.920 --> 02:15.670
Here. You left it by the sink.

02:17.900 --> 02:21.660
<b>Saturday, April 13</b>

02:17.900 --> 02:21.660
<b></b>Message

02:17.900 --> 02:21.660
<b></b>2 mins ago

02:17.900 --> 02:21.660
Oushi
Missed video call

02:19.140 --> 02:21.660
<i>Oushi-kun? Why?</i>

02:23.190 --> 02:27.330
Everything okay? 
Tell me if you have any issues.

02:27.610 --> 02:30.650
<i>He saw the notification.</i>

02:31.330 --> 02:32.920
<b></b>I'll be fine

02:31.330 --> 02:32.920
<b></b>I'll be fine

02:33.330 --> 02:34.120
Cool.

02:36.090 --> 02:37.720
Missed call

02:36.090 --> 02:37.720
Sorry about that.

02:37.590 --> 02:39.220
Missed call

02:37.590 --> 02:39.220
Sorry about that.

02:37.590 --> 02:39.220
I'll contact you again later.

02:39.220 --> 02:44.220
<b>Yuki, you fool</b>

02:39.220 --> 02:44.220
<b>fool







fool</b>

02:39.220 --> 02:44.220
<b>fool











fool</b>

02:39.220 --> 02:44.220
<b>fool</b>

02:39.220 --> 02:44.220
<b>fool</b>

02:39.610 --> 02:41.560
<i>Oushi-kun's apologizing?!</i>

02:42.060 --> 02:44.220
<i>That's actually kinda scary.</i>

02:52.220 --> 02:55.980
<i>Different shampoo and body soap 
than I have at home.</i>

03:02.130 --> 03:02.990
<i>Huh?</i>

03:03.940 --> 03:05.330
<i>Where's Itsuomi-san?</i>

03:06.540 --> 03:07.650
Yuki.

03:08.990 --> 03:09.870
In here.

03:12.900 --> 03:15.810
<i>Is this his bedroom?</i>

03:16.250 --> 03:18.940
Your phone's over there.

03:21.410 --> 03:23.320
Don't be so nervous.

03:23.910 --> 03:25.260
Want some popcorn?

03:25.600 --> 03:29.550
<i>Oh my god... I can't take much more of this.</i>

03:30.680 --> 03:31.540
Look.

03:32.420 --> 03:35.010
Whenever I have time on weekends, it's...

03:35.510 --> 03:40.290
Movie... Night.

03:41.080 --> 03:42.150
What do you wanna watch?

03:43.450 --> 03:46.410
If we turn on subtitles, 
we can watch together.

03:47.370 --> 03:48.890
<i>Itsuomi-san...</i>

03:51.790 --> 03:52.920
<b>Mute</b>

03:55.150 --> 03:58.420
I was wondering how it normally 
feels for you to watch a movie.

03:59.020 --> 04:00.920
Feel free to doze off whenever.

04:01.300 --> 04:05.140
<i>N-No way I can sleep in this situation!</i>

04:13.690 --> 04:17.060
<b>Madoka
Video Call</b>

04:22.550 --> 04:23.950
<i>Madoka-chan!</i>

04:26.120 --> 04:27.280
<i>Yuki!</i>

04:27.610 --> 04:29.330
<i>Sorry I took so long!</i>

04:29.660 --> 04:31.080
<i>You doing okay?</i>

04:32.190 --> 04:33.660
She's talking?

04:34.900 --> 04:36.490
High-speed signing!

04:36.490 --> 04:38.250
<i>Yeah, I'm doing super!</i>

04:42.220 --> 04:44.980
<i>Wait, your boyfriend? 
You have a boyfriend now?!</i>

04:44.980 --> 04:46.350
<i>Way to go!</i>

04:47.010 --> 04:48.420
Nice to meet you.

04:48.420 --> 04:50.460
<i>Huh? You can sign?</i>

04:50.460 --> 04:54.590
<i>Wait, I'm not good at lipreading. 
I've got late-onset hearing loss!</i>

04:54.590 --> 04:57.400
<i>Oh, sorry for rambling!</i>

04:57.400 --> 05:00.650
<i>By the way, Yuki. 
Looks like the job thing is a go.</i>

05:00.650 --> 05:01.690
<b></b>Really?!

05:00.650 --> 05:01.690
<b></b>Really?!

05:01.690 --> 05:04.110
<i>I asked my aunt, and she said sure!</i>

05:04.500 --> 05:07.540
<i>She said she'd like help in the kitchen.</i>

05:07.540 --> 05:12.110
<i>The owner's my aunt, 
and she can sign a bit. So you can relax.</i>

05:12.110 --> 05:14.250
<i>I'll let you know when the interview will be.</i>

05:14.650 --> 05:16.340
<i>Talk to you later!</i>

05:18.550 --> 05:22.980
Can you read her lips? She talks really fast.

05:23.260 --> 05:25.130
<b></b>I watch her sign.

05:23.260 --> 05:25.130
<b></b>I watch her sign.

05:25.510 --> 05:27.380
She does have a motor mouth.

05:27.630 --> 05:35.140
Madoka-chan lost her hearing late,
and she doesn't want to forget how
to speak. So she talks and signs
simultaneously at all times.

05:31.530 --> 05:33.180
Oh, wow.

05:33.180 --> 05:35.140
There's all types, huh?

05:35.690 --> 05:38.620
That aside, glad to hear about the job.

05:40.730 --> 05:42.150
When I'm with you,

05:42.270 --> 05:52.160
even a job

05:43.900 --> 05:52.160
which seemed a long-term goal before

05:46.150 --> 05:52.160
happens instantly.

05:47.660 --> 05:49.960
Nah, it was all you.

05:50.790 --> 05:54.050
<i>Itsuomi-san leads the way</i>

05:52.160 --> 05:56.040
<b></b>Come on! I wanna show you something over here!

05:54.740 --> 05:57.460
<i>and takes me to all kinds of new places.</i>

05:56.370 --> 05:58.420
<b></b>I've never come this far before.

06:26.440 --> 06:27.130
Yuki...

06:28.600 --> 06:30.390
You're really tense.

06:44.280 --> 06:47.190
Don't get so nervous when we're cuddling.

06:50.770 --> 06:52.090
What a pleasant surprise.

06:53.470 --> 06:55.850
You asking me to come out on a day off.

06:56.180 --> 06:59.740
Sorry about that. Did you have plans?

06:59.740 --> 07:03.130
Nah, I just got back, so good timing.

07:04.340 --> 07:05.360
What's the matter?

07:08.260 --> 07:09.490
Is this about Emma-chan?

07:11.890 --> 07:15.490
I couldn't tell her. 
We just had dinner and split.

07:16.190 --> 07:21.550
I get it. Hearing Itsu has a girlfriend now 
would make her really sad, after all.

07:22.650 --> 07:26.210
Is there a way to break the news 
to her without hurting her?

07:27.320 --> 07:29.430
You know, I always wanted to ask.

07:29.840 --> 07:32.730
The girl you love is in love 
with your best friend.

07:32.730 --> 07:35.230
Did that not make you hate Itsu?

07:35.720 --> 07:38.020
I mean, he's a great guy.

07:38.730 --> 07:42.490
So you care about them both, huh?

07:42.490 --> 07:44.050
Well, duh.

07:44.990 --> 07:46.530
How about yourself?

07:46.530 --> 07:47.020
Huh?

07:48.760 --> 07:51.990
You can't go neglecting 
your own feelings all the time.

08:00.370 --> 08:02.000
<i>I can't sleep...</i>

08:02.450 --> 08:08.020
<i>Regular couples out there usually sleep 
in the same bed at these times, don't they?</i>

08:09.450 --> 08:14.870
<i>Is this what he meant by "We're just 
gonna be spending time together"?</i>

08:18.260 --> 08:20.520
I'm really happy I got to spend
all day with you.

08:23.770 --> 08:26.020
Is this different from "staying over,"
though?

08:29.240 --> 08:30.620
<i>Itsuomi-san.</i>

08:32.210 --> 08:33.930
We can save that for later.

08:36.420 --> 08:39.850
You still get so tense 
when we're just cuddling.

08:41.330 --> 08:43.330
You're important to me,

08:45.210 --> 08:48.500
so I want to treat you right.

08:52.630 --> 08:54.660
<i>This is going to be a sleepless night.</i>

08:55.470 --> 08:58.300
<i>But I'm okay with that.</i>

08:58.810 --> 09:01.780
<i>Because, if I take out my 
hearing aids and fall asleep,</i>

09:01.780 --> 09:05.970
<i>this moment will simply disappear forever.</i>

09:07.540 --> 09:13.930
<i>Itsuomi-san's bedroom is like 
a treasure box filled to the brim,</i>

09:14.500 --> 09:16.820
<i>and I want it to remain in my memories.</i>

09:30.210 --> 09:33.210
<b></b>You, what are you playing at?

09:30.210 --> 09:33.210
<b></b>You, what are you playing at?

09:36.420 --> 09:38.140
You understand that, right?

09:38.610 --> 09:42.850
I heard you can sign a little. 
And that you're dating Yuki.

09:45.220 --> 09:47.120
Can we skip all this bullshit?

09:47.120 --> 09:50.860
What, you think you're better 
because you're going out with her?

09:51.400 --> 09:54.340
You're misunderstanding something.

09:54.340 --> 09:55.110
Huh?

09:55.440 --> 10:00.610
Fine. I figured I'd have 
to talk to you eventually.

10:01.720 --> 10:02.770
You got time?

10:02.770 --> 10:04.440
What's it to you?

10:05.250 --> 10:09.710
C'mon, let's play nice here, Oushi-kun.

10:10.000 --> 10:11.320
Say wha?!

10:14.690 --> 10:16.510
Hey, wait!

10:16.890 --> 10:18.630
You listening to me?!

10:19.000 --> 10:20.780
Let me go, damn it!

10:22.300 --> 10:23.310
Dude, lemme go!

10:23.700 --> 10:25.400
Isn't that Oushi?

10:25.400 --> 10:26.740
Sure is.

10:26.740 --> 10:29.190
What is he even doing?

10:29.190 --> 10:30.930
You ass...

10:30.930 --> 10:32.090
Hey, Itsuomi!

10:33.490 --> 10:34.320
Hey.

10:34.320 --> 10:35.690
Is he your friend?

10:34.320 --> 10:35.690
<b></b>Is he your friend?

10:34.320 --> 10:35.690
<b></b>Is he your friend?

10:35.820 --> 10:37.690
No, not yet.

10:35.820 --> 10:37.690
<b></b>No, not yet.

10:35.820 --> 10:37.690
<b></b>No, not yet.

10:37.940 --> 10:40.280
Really? I hope you can get along with him.

10:37.940 --> 10:40.280
<b></b>Really? I hope you can get along with him.

10:37.940 --> 10:40.280
<b></b>Really? I hope you can get along with him.

10:40.700 --> 10:42.030
Thanks. See ya.

10:40.700 --> 10:42.030
<b></b>Thanks. See ya.

10:40.700 --> 10:42.030
<b></b>Thanks. See ya.

10:42.570 --> 10:44.330
Itsu! Was machst du?

10:42.570 --> 10:44.330
<b></b>Itsu? What're you doing?

10:42.570 --> 10:44.330
<b></b>Itsu? What're you doing?

10:44.950 --> 10:47.830
Ich werde in Zukunft mit ihm auskommen.

10:44.950 --> 10:47.830
<b></b>Trying to get friendly with this guy.

10:44.950 --> 10:47.830
<b></b>Trying to get friendly with this guy.

10:47.830 --> 10:48.780
Ach so!

10:49.470 --> 10:50.710
Itsu.

10:50.990 --> 10:52.210
Itsu!

10:52.600 --> 10:53.960
Itsu!

10:56.710 --> 10:59.220
<b>Cultural Exchange Club</b>

10:59.480 --> 11:01.650
Whew, that wore me out.

11:06.470 --> 11:07.720
Oh, that?

11:08.150 --> 11:11.460
We put on a Japanese period drama 
in English for the college fest last year.

11:12.620 --> 11:15.570
What do you wanna talk about 
that has to be in here?

11:16.620 --> 11:18.860
Oushi, tell me...

11:19.420 --> 11:21.360
What's your favorite bread at Komugi?

11:22.890 --> 11:25.050
K-Komugi?

11:25.050 --> 11:26.990
The bakery outside campus?

11:26.990 --> 11:28.250
It's the curry bread for me.

11:28.520 --> 11:32.320
Why do I gotta tell you my bread preferences?

11:32.320 --> 11:34.000
Favorite dish in the cafeteria, then?

11:34.000 --> 11:34.690
Wha?!

11:35.440 --> 11:38.560
What club are you in? Play any sports?

11:38.560 --> 11:40.420
Which faculty? What's your favorite class?

11:40.420 --> 11:41.510
Stop that.

11:41.900 --> 11:46.540
I hate you. And I have no idea why 
you're asking me these questions.

11:46.540 --> 11:47.850
You're creeping me out.

11:48.580 --> 11:50.370
Why do you hate me?

11:50.370 --> 11:51.100
Huh?

11:51.500 --> 11:52.750
C'mon, tell me.

11:52.750 --> 11:55.400
What do you hate about me, and why?

11:55.400 --> 11:57.980
What is with your attitude, dude?!

11:58.570 --> 12:00.350
Anyway, I got things to do.

12:01.090 --> 12:04.910
Gimme something to work with here. 
All I know about you is your name.

12:06.330 --> 12:07.370
What else...

12:08.030 --> 12:10.360
You're in love with Yuki, right?

12:15.060 --> 12:16.440
It's not like that.

12:17.920 --> 12:23.210
The reason I hate you is because 
you provoked me at the station back then.

12:23.630 --> 12:28.520
Also, you're crazy for asking a girl who 
can't hear to come see you so late at night.

12:29.930 --> 12:33.560
And who knows how many times 
you've bleached your hair?

12:34.370 --> 12:36.810
You're weird, and I want 
nothing to do with you.

12:36.810 --> 12:38.200
There you go. Happy now?

12:46.550 --> 12:48.480
Why are you following me?!

12:48.480 --> 12:51.290
I mean, I'm not done talking.

12:51.290 --> 12:53.370
Well, <i>we're</i> done!

12:53.370 --> 12:57.290
And even if we weren't, there's no 
getting through your thick skull!

12:57.770 --> 13:01.360
Man, your mood swings 
are something else, you know that?

13:01.360 --> 13:03.300
It's <i>your</i> damn fault!

13:03.720 --> 13:07.080
Looks like this is gonna take a while.

13:07.080 --> 13:08.010
What are you talking—

13:08.010 --> 13:11.820
Come to the campus front gate at 7 PM tonight.

13:11.820 --> 13:12.890
Why?!

13:13.610 --> 13:16.900
If you do, I'll do anything you want.

13:17.280 --> 13:18.260
You mean it?

13:19.060 --> 13:20.690
Nothing sexual, though.

13:21.480 --> 13:24.150
Are you stupid? I'm <i>not</i> going!

13:27.580 --> 13:31.730
I work here part-time. This here's my cousin.

13:31.730 --> 13:34.660
Welcome. Do you two go to the same college?

13:34.920 --> 13:37.250
This is Oushi, Yuki's childhood friend.

13:37.250 --> 13:39.640
He's going through his 
misanthrope arc right now.

13:39.640 --> 13:41.170
Don't go running your mouth.

13:41.910 --> 13:43.000
Beer for me.

13:43.650 --> 13:45.340
Are you old enough to drink?

13:45.340 --> 13:47.680
I am, but I'm not drinking with you.

13:52.010 --> 13:55.270
Who opens a bottle that way? 
You trying to show off?

13:55.830 --> 13:58.660
Bottle openers aren't used 
too much in Germany.

13:58.660 --> 13:59.550
Germany?

14:00.420 --> 14:02.110
That's where I grew up.

14:02.570 --> 14:06.030
I drank my first beer 
on my sixteenth birthday.

14:06.780 --> 14:09.900
In Germany, you're allowed to drink 
at that age if you're with a parent.

14:11.580 --> 14:13.150
I'll have a beer too, please.

14:13.660 --> 14:15.720
<i>I told ya so.</i>

14:15.720 --> 14:19.150
<i>Kiddos should stick to milk.</i>

14:19.150 --> 14:21.920
<i>I'm not a kid! I'm eleven!</i>

14:25.110 --> 14:25.920
Yum.

14:26.420 --> 14:28.310
Don't chug booze on an empty stomach.

14:28.760 --> 14:30.200
Here, have this. It's good.

14:30.870 --> 14:33.090
How many languages can you speak?

14:34.060 --> 14:35.300
Three.

14:36.030 --> 14:38.850
Japanese, German, and English.

14:39.420 --> 14:40.940
Oh, really.

14:41.410 --> 14:44.420
"Why's someone like you 
trying to pick up sign language"?

14:46.730 --> 14:48.900
You know why. For the same reason as you.

14:49.650 --> 14:52.350
I'm not like you, you gray-haired ass.

14:52.350 --> 14:55.290
I'm letting a stylist buddy 
experiment on my hair.

14:55.870 --> 14:57.930
Next time we meet, I might have an afro.

14:59.500 --> 15:00.780
You okay?

15:00.780 --> 15:02.620
Don't make me laugh, damn you...

15:28.850 --> 15:30.510
Oh, you're up.

15:31.450 --> 15:33.870
You passed out after your third beer.

15:34.310 --> 15:37.210
It's 1 AM now. Everyone's gone.

15:39.260 --> 15:41.740
Oh, my tab.

15:41.740 --> 15:44.660
On the house tonight, apparently. You sick?

15:49.070 --> 15:49.990
I'm leaving.

15:50.680 --> 15:52.300
Hey, hold up!

15:54.560 --> 15:56.910
I knew it. You can barely walk.

15:57.370 --> 16:00.580
I don't wanna see your name on the 
morning news tomorrow, you hear?

16:02.230 --> 16:03.090
Oushi?

16:03.690 --> 16:04.820
You...

16:05.660 --> 16:09.480
Stay away. Don't get in my space.

16:10.170 --> 16:10.970
What?

16:11.790 --> 16:15.950
Did you think learning sign language 
would make her an easy target?

16:17.370 --> 16:21.090
I didn't pick up sign for 
such a manipulative reason.

16:26.110 --> 16:31.730
Why do we gotta go to Bon dance practice 
when it's summer break, Sis?

16:31.730 --> 16:37.430
Again, if we kids put on a performance 
at the festival, we get snacks for free.

16:37.430 --> 16:40.090
Yeah, well, I bet they'll be 
nothing special, anyway.

16:40.910 --> 16:42.380
Oh, quiet!

16:42.380 --> 16:44.980
Don't irritate me. It's too hot for this.

16:45.860 --> 16:48.110
Oh, Yuki-chan.

16:48.110 --> 16:49.110
Who?

16:49.550 --> 16:51.530
She's the same age as you.

16:51.530 --> 16:53.870
I've never seen her in school, though.

16:53.870 --> 16:56.360
She goes to a school for the deaf.

16:56.360 --> 17:00.620
<b>Picture Book of Flowers</b>

16:56.710 --> 16:58.200
What's that?

16:58.550 --> 17:00.620
Yuki-chan can't hear.

17:00.940 --> 17:01.720
What?!

17:02.220 --> 17:03.210
Wait for me here.

17:05.690 --> 17:07.000
Hello there.

17:10.880 --> 17:13.130
<b>Fun Sign Language Learning</b>

17:22.120 --> 17:25.650
Whoa! Isn't it beautiful, Oushi?

17:25.650 --> 17:28.690
What's fun about fireworks? 
They're just loud and smoky.

17:28.690 --> 17:29.520
Huh?

17:29.520 --> 17:31.780
What was that? I couldn't hear you!

17:47.370 --> 17:49.210
You

17:50.450 --> 17:51.910
<i>If I signed...</i>

17:52.820 --> 17:54.470
<i>When I was signing...</i>

17:56.310 --> 17:59.390
<i>she looked my way.</i>

17:58.430 --> 18:00.220
fool.

18:01.100 --> 18:03.530
<i>No matter how noisy our surroundings were,</i>

18:03.970 --> 18:05.560
<b></b>"You fool"?!

18:03.970 --> 18:05.560
<b></b>"You fool"?!

18:04.410 --> 18:07.530
<i>we could enter our own little world 
where nothing could bother us.</i>

18:06.100 --> 18:06.940
<b></b>Wait...

18:06.100 --> 18:06.940
<b></b>Wait...

18:06.980 --> 18:08.690
<b></b>You can sign?

18:06.980 --> 18:08.690
<b></b>You can sign?

18:08.980 --> 18:13.980
<b>Fun Sign Language Learning</b>

18:09.400 --> 18:13.400
<i>It was like our own little secret code.</i>

18:16.990 --> 18:19.740
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

18:16.990 --> 18:19.740
<b>Illustrated and Photo Guide
Sign Language for Beginners</b>

18:16.990 --> 18:19.740
<b></b>\h\hLearn more about the world of sign language\h\h

18:17.370 --> 18:20.440
<i>The expressions and emotions born within</i>

18:19.740 --> 18:21.240
<b>Yummy Bakery</b>

18:21.520 --> 18:24.240
<i>were no different to what 
the spoken word can create,</i>

18:24.240 --> 18:25.650
<i>but it still felt special.</i>

18:27.060 --> 18:30.260
<i>And I got more and more 
hooked on sign language.</i>

18:32.580 --> 18:34.750
Hey, you okay there?

18:36.230 --> 18:38.910
If you're sick, you can rest up inside.

18:39.790 --> 18:41.820
Nah, I'm going home.

18:47.480 --> 18:48.690
Nearly forgot.

18:49.460 --> 18:51.900
You said you'd do anything I wanted.

18:52.500 --> 18:55.650
I like your spirit. Well, what'll it be?

18:57.730 --> 19:00.170
Break up with Yuki.

19:00.870 --> 19:01.820
Listen, man.

19:02.210 --> 19:05.220
Breaking up is a mutual decision.

19:06.300 --> 19:08.280
And Yuki won't break up with me.

19:08.280 --> 19:11.380
Huh? What's with that confidence?

19:11.380 --> 19:14.330
Confidence isn't something you're born with. 
You gotta build it yourself.

19:14.330 --> 19:16.920
And you gotta build trust in a relationship.

19:18.980 --> 19:23.060
I know you're popular, so why her? 
Any girl would choose you in a heartbeat.

19:23.660 --> 19:26.430
Why does it matter who chooses me?

19:27.250 --> 19:32.560
At a glance, Yuki and I are so different 
that we might not even look like friends.

19:33.700 --> 19:37.110
But she was there in a space 
that was surprisingly close to me.

19:38.090 --> 19:42.570
And that was only possible 
because she chose to go to college.

19:42.840 --> 19:45.610
So I'm glad she made that choice.

19:47.020 --> 19:53.510
Well, even if she hadn't, we'd have met 
somewhere years down the line.

19:54.250 --> 19:55.340
What're you trying to say?

20:00.210 --> 20:05.500
It wouldn't matter when or where we met.

20:05.810 --> 20:08.100
I'd fall for Yuki and choose her every time.

20:21.660 --> 20:26.460
<i>I didn't want these feelings of mine 
to be boxed into any old category.</i>

20:28.930 --> 20:30.120
<i>Oh, man...</i>

20:31.170 --> 20:32.050
<i>Don't look.</i>

20:33.050 --> 20:34.110
<i>Stop looking.</i>

20:35.950 --> 20:38.850
<i>Quit looking at another guy's hands.</i>

20:41.000 --> 20:44.300
I like the curry bread, too.

20:44.980 --> 20:45.590
Huh?

20:45.860 --> 20:50.550
My favorite Komugi bread! 
You asked me earlier!

20:50.550 --> 20:52.640
Oh. Hey, we have similar tastes.

20:52.640 --> 20:55.650
Sure, you may be dating at the moment,

20:55.650 --> 20:58.440
but it's not as easy as you think!

21:00.070 --> 21:02.400
You really can't do anything 
but slam on the brakes, huh?

21:02.400 --> 21:04.450
And you're nothing but pedal to the metal!

21:04.860 --> 21:08.990
Listen, I'm not into taking 
another guy's girlfriend!

21:08.990 --> 21:10.360
Hurry up and break up!

21:11.750 --> 21:14.220
I expected this to be more complicated,

21:14.670 --> 21:16.960
but it looks like taking one piece 
will make the puzzle crumble.

21:25.340 --> 21:27.210
What's... going on?

21:27.210 --> 21:28.900
You're a mess, huh?

21:29.210 --> 21:29.890
Damn it...

21:35.300 --> 21:38.270
Man, for some reason,

21:38.990 --> 21:40.650
I can't bring myself to hate you.

21:42.320 --> 21:43.400
If...

21:43.950 --> 21:46.600
If you ever make her cry...

21:49.620 --> 21:53.750
then, taken or not, I'll come for her!

21:55.080 --> 21:57.750
Well, I'm not planning on that.

21:58.830 --> 22:01.960
<i>Maybe I can change. Maybe I already have.</i>

22:02.970 --> 22:07.160
<i>But either way, I don't wanna let this guy 
beat me without a fight.</i>

22:06.010 --> 22:10.010
Oushi's World

23:15.030 --> 23:30.260
Promise
